PAD-1090: add Linux spidev ioctl translation to qemu-user (on top of
qemu-i2c-ioctls.patch). The spidev settings (mode, lsb-first, bits per
word, max speed, mode32) by pointer, and SPI_IOC_MESSAGE(1..16) through a
nested-pointer handler that maps each transfer's guest tx/rx buffers.
Without it the CPU board's SPI I/O chain (/dev/spidev4.0) answers ENOTTY.

Apply after the i2c patch, to the same pristine qemu 8.2.2 tree:
    cd qemu-8.2.2 && patch -p1 < qemu-i2c-ioctls.patch
    patch -p1 < qemu-spi-ioctls.patch

